            stem: "A subcontractor and a general contractor signed a contract providing that any dispute 'shall be litigated exclusively in the federal court for the District of State X.' The subcontractor sued the general contractor in a federal district court in State Y, where venue would otherwise be proper under §1391(b). The general contractor moved to dismiss for improper venue under 28 U.S.C. §1406(a) and Rule 12(b)(3), pointing to the clause. The clause is valid and enforceable.",
